1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,970
Resumes tell you what candidates have done.

2
00:00:02,970 --> 00:00:03,750
Interviews tell you

3
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:05,850
how well they present themselves.

4
00:00:05,850 --> 00:00:07,530
But neither necessarily shows

5
00:00:07,530 --> 00:00:09,780
how they perform when the work gets real.

6
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:14,080
That’s where VibeLevel Screening comes in.

7
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:16,940
Through realistic, role-specific tasks,

8
00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:20,100
it evaluates candidates across four dimensions:

9
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:22,680
Core Skills, Working with AI, Ownership,

10
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:23,670
and Human Contribution.

11
00:00:25,110 --> 00:00:26,710
Candidates tackle these tasks

12
00:00:26,710 --> 00:00:28,130
in a dedicated workspace

13
00:00:28,130 --> 00:00:31,630
with AI coding tools such as Claude Code,

14
00:00:31,630 --> 00:00:34,750
Codex, GitHub Copilot, and more built in.

15
00:00:34,750 --> 00:00:37,270
As they work through real challenges,

16
00:00:37,270 --> 00:00:38,570
VibeLevel looks beyond the

17
00:00:38,570 --> 00:00:40,290
final output to understand

18
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:43,220
how they solve problems and collaborate with AI.

19
00:00:44,210 --> 00:00:45,050
First,

20
00:00:45,050 --> 00:00:47,350
Core Skills shows how well candidates apply

21
00:00:47,350 --> 00:00:49,710
their technical knowledge to the task.

22
00:00:49,710 --> 00:00:51,010
Working with AI reveals

23
00:00:51,010 --> 00:00:53,530
how effectively they guide AI,

24
00:00:53,530 --> 00:00:56,460
evaluate its suggestions, and verify the results.

25
00:00:57,350 --> 00:01:00,630
But technical ability is only part of the picture.

26
00:01:00,630 --> 00:01:02,790
Ownership reveals how candidates take

27
00:01:02,790 --> 00:01:05,170
responsibility for their decisions,

28
00:01:05,170 --> 00:01:07,710
while Human Contribution highlights the judgment

29
00:01:07,710 --> 00:01:11,300
and value they bring beyond AI-generated output.

30
00:01:12,230 --> 00:01:14,150
To evaluate the right skills,

31
00:01:14,150 --> 00:01:15,150
recruiters can start

32
00:01:15,150 --> 00:01:17,550
with ready-made assessment templates,

33
00:01:17,550 --> 00:01:19,870
customize them to their role requirements,

34
00:01:19,870 --> 00:01:22,030
or use AI to create assessments

35
00:01:22,030 --> 00:01:24,790
by simply describing what they need.

36
00:01:24,790 --> 00:01:26,450
And these assessments can integrate

37
00:01:26,450 --> 00:01:30,230
with ATS platforms such as Lever and Ashby,

38
00:01:30,230 --> 00:01:31,470
fitting directly into their

39
00:01:31,470 --> 00:01:33,060
existing hiring workflow.

40
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:36,540
Once candidates complete their assessments,

41
00:01:36,540 --> 00:01:38,200
recruiters get a clearer picture of

42
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:40,460
their performance through skill scores,

43
00:01:40,460 --> 00:01:43,480
AI collaboration insights, Code Review,

44
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:45,000
and Video Q&A.

45
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,580
The Interview Guide then turns those findings

46
00:01:47,580 --> 00:01:49,960
into focused follow-up questions,

47
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:51,840
helping recruiters explore strengths

48
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:53,490
and gaps in greater depth.

49
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:57,720
With a clearer view of how candidates think, work,

50
00:01:57,720 --> 00:02:00,580
and use AI, you can identify strengths,

51
00:02:00,580 --> 00:02:01,580
uncover gaps,

52
00:02:01,580 --> 00:02:03,610
and build a shortlist backed by evidence.

53
00:02:04,820 --> 00:02:06,360
When AI can do the work,

54
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:08,940
know what makes a candidate stand out,

55
00:02:08,940 --> 00:02:10,949
across developer and non-developer roles.

56
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:13,840
VibeLevel Screening.

57
